# Architecture Documentation Reminder

When making changes to **structural or architectural code** (entities, DB migrations, config, security, enums), check whether the change warrants an architecture doc update.

## When to act

- New entity or significant changes to an existing entity
- New Flyway migration that alters schema (new tables, column changes, enum types)
- Changes to security configuration (auth flow, filters, role definitions)
- New enum types or changes to existing ones
- Changes to Spring configuration (CORS, profiles, bean definitions)

## What to do

1. Check `docs/architecture/` for an existing doc covering this area
2. If one exists, update it with the new decision or change
3. If none exists and the change is significant, create a new ADR using the template at `docs/architecture/_TEMPLATE.md`
4. Name new ADRs as `ADR-XXX-short-title.md` (increment the number from the highest existing ADR)
5. Update `docs/README.md` index with a link to the new doc

## ADR fields to fill

- **Status**: Set to `Accepted`
- **Date**: Today's date
- **Domain**: The feature area (enrollment, auth, group-insurance, etc.)
- **Context**: Why this decision was needed
- **Decision**: What was decided
- **Consequences**: What this enables or limits

## Ask the user

> "This change affects [area]. Should I create/update an architecture decision record in `docs/architecture/`?"
